    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2YWjtKsLbFBfV3ynQseWxLE)_\n\n## What\n`sp-minibuffer` (sp-fonts) scales every minibuffer up two `text-scale` steps from `minibuffer-mode-hook`. The posframe shows that buffer, so its text size came from that scale. New `sp-posframe--reset-text-scale` runs later on `minibuffer-setup-hook` (depth 90) and sets the scale to 0 when `vertico-posframe-mode` is on, so every posframe prompt uses the size of the `default` face. Prompts outside the posframe (`read-string`, `y-or-n-p`) keep the larger size. Doc and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n## Not tested\nNothing was run in Emacs (none in the container). I did not find why the note pickers differed from `M-x` specifically; this makes all posframe prompts equal regardless. If they still differ, tell me which one is off.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9cVX4xhp367pqb88n)_",
